===Etymology===
From {{compound|is|orð|t1=word|bók|t2=book}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈɔrðaˌpou̯ːk/|[ˈɔ̝rð̠˕äˌpou̯ːk]}}
*: {{rhymes|is|ɔrðapouːk|apouːk|ouːk}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|f,,^ur}}

# A [[dictionary]] ''or'' [[wordbook]]; a publication — online or physical — which lists (often in alphabetical order) the words ''and/or'' phrases of a language ''or'' languages with provided definitions or clarification of meaning.
#: {{ux|is|[[ég|Ég]] [[munu|myndi]] [[aldrei]] [[treysta]] [[sá|þeirri]] '''orðabók''', [[hún]] [[vera|er]] [[fullur|full]] [[af]] [[hræðilegur|hræðilegum]] [[skilgreining|skilgreiningum]].|I would never trust that '''dictionary''', it’s full of terrible definitions.}}
#: {{syn|is|orðsifjabók}}
# A [[lexicon]]; the vocabulary of a person, institution, language, ''or'' branch of knowledge.
#: {{ux|is|[[enginn|Enginn]] [[vera|er]] [[í raun]] [[viss]] [[um]] [[hvort]] „[[köttur]]“ [[vera|sé]] [[hluti]] [[af]] '''orðabókinni''' [[sem]] [[dýrafræðingur|dýrafræðingar]] [[nota]].|No one is really sure as to whether or not “cat” is a part of the '''lexicon''' which zoologists use.}}

